course: dictionary
lesson: 568
title: The aura of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aura is a special feeling or quality that seems to surround a person or place, like an air of calm, mystery or importance. You can often sense it before anyone says a word. A story might describe a character with an aura of danger, and the reader feels it from the way they are described.
explain: Look at the words around aura to find its meaning. In the slang sentence «aura» means cool points, so the clue is the list of other slang words: rizz means charm, mid means average, and fr means for real. These are all words used by young people to talk about how someone seems.
explain: Aura can also mean a soft glow of light around someone or something, as in old pictures of saints or in magical stories. Doctors use the word too: some people with migraines see strange lights or feel tingles just before the headache starts. The meaning depends on the sentence around it.
fact: Aura means a special feeling or quality that seems to surround a person or place.
fact: An aura can also be a soft glow of light around someone or something.
fact: In medicine, an aura is strange lights, tingles or feelings that come just before a migraine or a fit.
fact: Some people believe everyone has a coloured aura that only special people can see; science has found no evidence for this.
fact: Phrases to try: an aura of mystery, an aura of calm, an aura about her.
exercise: «The old house had an aura of mystery, and nobody went near it.» What does aura mean here? | A type of old paint | *A special feeling that seems to surround the house | A list of rules for visitors | A loud noise from the attic
exercise: In old paintings, saints often have a soft golden glow around their heads. What is that glow called? | A migraine | *An aura | A sneeze | A castle
exercise: Mia says, «She has an aura of calm.» What does Mia mean? | She is shouting at everyone | She is lost in the city | She is feeling unwell | *She seems peaceful and steady
test: Before her headache, Sara saw flashing lights in the corner of her eyes. Doctors call this warning sign an | Echo | Shadow | *Aura | Mood
test: «The room had an aura of calm.» What does this tell you? | The room was loud and crowded | *The room felt peaceful | The room was on fire | Yellow paint covered the walls
exam: Jayden says aura means cool points in the slang sentence. Is he right, and how can he check? | No, aura only ever means a glow of light | No, it means a type of magic spell | Yes, but only in science lessons | *Yes, the other slang words around it give the clue, and he can swap in cool points to see if it fits
